  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "At Eastern Sea Gu tribe headquarters, during a banquet of immortal chickens, Gu tribe’s leader inhales a millstone-sized roasted ancient desolate chicken in one swallow. His stomach bulges. He says the chicken needs half a day more to digest, and that during that time his luck is strengthened.",
      "chapters": [
        1871
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "reg_eastern_sea",
        "fac_gu_tribe"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Wu Shuai, Fang Yuan’s clone, calls the luck strengthening an exceptional food path method that produces a luck path effect, and judges that it emphasizes survival. Gu tribe’s leader agrees. Historical records of his tribe say this move is why their Gu Immortals survived dangerous situations and large scale battle royale.",
      "chapters": [
        1871
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_wu_shuai",
        "char_fang_yuan",
        "sys_gu_immortal"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The display is one content of Gu tribe’s food path inheritance, which generations modified. Beastmen name killer moves simply and crudely, with practical effects. Fang Yuan later notes Chicken Dinner among the inheritance’s creative methods as a move that can imitate luck path effect.",
